+# myrmidon(G1): how many times in a row the same model call is re-issued after an HTTP-200
+# ``content_filter`` refusal before the refusal ends the turn. The refusal need not repeat for an
+# unchanged long context (the filter cut a harmless reply mid-word), and the work done so far lives
+# in the session, so a re-issue costs one model call, not the run. The streak restarts after a
+# model call that was not refused. ``_CONTENT_FILTER_RETRIES_PER_TURN`` caps the re-issues of the
+# whole turn, so an input that is blocked again and again cannot burn calls without end.
+_CONTENT_FILTER_RETRIES = 2
+_CONTENT_FILTER_RETRIES_PER_TURN = 8
+
 _THINKING_EXHAUSTED = (
